<p>NOTE - Non-recurring items, net of tax, in respect of 1996 include: i) a non-cash charge of $720.9 million in Q1 1996, relating to the write-down of specific assets to their estimated fair values in accordance with the requirements of SFAS 121; ii) a charge of $195 million principally relating to costs associated with integrating the businesses of ASH in Britain and the United States into ADT, together with the costs of administrative, accounting, management information and technological infrastructure enhancements currently being implemented in the United States electronic security services division; iii) a gain of $53.4 million, represented by cash, arising on the sale of the company's entire interest in Limelight Group Plc, which was recorded in the balance sheet at a nominal value; and iv)  a gain of $69.7 million represented by cash receivable as a result of the settlement of the company's litigation against Binder Hamlyn</p>
